MIT is the shorter and simpler of the two, and is compatible with GPLv2.
Apache-2.0 additionally grants an explicit patent licence, which some adopters
require.

Unless you state otherwise, any contribution you intentionally submit for
inclusion in this work shall be dual-licensed as above, without any additional
terms or conditions.

Scriptor also bundles third-party components, most visibly the substitute fonts
in crates/scriptor-fonts/fonts/, which remain under their own licences. Two of
them are not what a reader who sees only "MIT OR Apache-2.0" would expect.
THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md lists them and their terms; it ships alongside this file.
